[B11's Example 7.4 (Parallel reduction)]

e,1,0,16.8
r1,1,2,9
r2,1,2,6
r3,2,3,4
re1,3,0,[6,3]
r6,2,0,3

analysis: dc
note: In this problem, we use the [,] parallel-reduction shorthand for the first time, folding the 6 and 3 ohm resistors into one equivalent; the same circuit was solved element by element in Lesson 1. Evaluate -ie for the current the source delivers: 3 A.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/b11s-example-7-4-8.jpg
rounding: approx
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: -ie


