[RM3's Example 9-12 (Step 1)]

e,0,b,20
r1,0,a,16
r2,a,b,40
r3,a,b,60

analysis: dc
note: Step 1 of a source-replacement problem: simulate the original circuit to learn the voltage drop (va-vb, on the Evaluate line: 12 V) and the current (0.2 A) that the replacement in Step 2 must preserve.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/rm3s-example-9-12-solve-13.jpg
rounding: 3
si: no
units: yes
evaluate: va-vb


[RM3's Example 9-12 (Step 2)]

e,0,b,20
r1,0,a,16
r2,a,b,40
r4,a,b,240
j,a,b,i4

analysis: dc
note: Step 2: R3 is replaced by a 240 ohm R4 and a current source of unknown value i4. Solving va-vb = 12 for i4 keeps the drop found in Step 1. Or solve `ir4+ij = 0.2` instead, for the same answer.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/practice/rm3s-example-9-12-solve-13.jpg
rounding: 3
si: no
units: yes
solve_equations: va-vb = 12
solve_unknowns: i4


